  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#46434\"], \"answer\": \"This has been requested before. PowerToys#46434 asks for CPU and GPU temperature readings in the Command Palette Dock, next to the existing CPU and Memory stats. That looks like the bar you mean. A contributor said in that ticket that Windows has no native way to read per-component temperatures. Reading them would need vendor-specific driver APIs or WMI, which they said won't be implemented. They are working on a pull request that adds a single thermal-zone temperature metric read through PDH. That metric may not match your CPU's actual temperature. Follow PowerToys#46434 for updates and add a thumbs-up there. Until that ships, use a third-party tool such as HWiNFO or Core Temp to see CPU temperature. Similar requests for the taskbar or desktop are in PowerToys#35623 and PowerToys#8433.\"}",
